{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["If perhaps she turned aside because of me — every 'if perhaps' (אולי) in Scripture means like 'if' (אם) and like 'were it that' (אילו). And the commentators who explain this one as like ״לולא התמהמהנו״ and like ״לולי ה׳״ and so forth — it is an error in their hands. Rather, its meaning is like: ״אולי יש תקוה״, ״אולי יחנן ה׳ צבאות״, ״אולי משגה הוא״. And so the angel said: Why did you strike your she-ass three times — you acted unjustly, for ״ותט לפני זה שלש רגלים״ — all her turnings-aside were before me but not because of me, for she did not pass me by." "If perhaps she turned aside because of me — that is: if she turned aside because of me and not before me, that is, if she had passed me by on the road beyond me — I would also have killed you, that is: you would not have been saved by the minor injury of the crushing of your leg, but I would have killed even you, and she would not have been lost, for I kept her alive, as she is still alive now, for she was not rebellious, but rather you were rebellious against me, you who struck your she-ass." "Also you — also I would have killed you. Like: ״וברכתם גם אותי״ — also you will bless me."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:50.289894801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}